---@class polar.CheckoutProductsCreate
---@field trial_interval? polar.TrialInterval|string|distilled.Null The interval unit for the trial period.
---@field trial_interval_count? number|distilled.Null The number of interval units for the trial period.
---@field metadata? polar.CheckoutProductsCreateMetadataMap Key-value object allowing you to store additional information. The key must be a string with a maximum length of **40 characters**. The value must be either: * A string with a maximum length of **500 characters** * An integer * A floating-point number * A boolean You can store up to **50 key-value pairs**.
---@field custom_field_data? polar.CheckoutProductsCreateCustomFieldDataMap Key-value object storing custom field values.
---@field discount_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the discount to apply to the checkout.
---@field allow_discount_codes? boolean Whether to allow the customer to apply discount codes. If you apply a discount through `discount_id`, it'll still be applied, but the customer won't be able to change it.
---@field require_billing_address? boolean Whether to require the customer to fill their full billing address, instead of just the country. Customers in the US will always be required to fill their full address, regardless of this setting. If you preset the billing address, this setting will be automatically set to `true`.
---@field amount? number|distilled.Null
---@field seats? number|distilled.Null Predefined number of seats (works with seat-based pricing only)
---@field min_seats? number|distilled.Null Minimum number of seats (works with seat-based pricing only)
---@field max_seats? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of seats (works with seat-based pricing only)
---@field units? number|distilled.Null Predefined number of units (works with unit-based pricing only)
---@field min_units? number|distilled.Null Minimum number of units (works with unit-based pricing only)
---@field max_units? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of units (works with unit-based pricing only)
---@field allow_trial? boolean Whether to enable the trial period for the checkout session. If `false`, the trial period will be disabled, even if the selected product has a trial configured.
---@field customer_id? string|distilled.Null ID of an existing customer in the organization. The customer data will be pre-filled in the checkout form. The resulting order will be linked to this customer.
---@field is_business_customer? boolean Whether the customer is a business or an individual. If `true`, the customer will be required to fill their full billing address and billing name.
---@field external_customer_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the customer in your system. If a matching customer exists on Polar, the resulting order will be linked to this customer. Otherwise, a new customer will be created with this external ID set.
---@field customer_name? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_email? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_ip_address? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_billing_name? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_billing_address? polar.AddressInput|distilled.Null
---@field customer_tax_id? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_metadata? polar.CheckoutProductsCreateCustomerMetadataMap Key-value object allowing you to store additional information that'll be copied to the created customer. The key must be a string with a maximum length of **40 characters**. The value must be either: * A string with a maximum length of **500 characters** * An integer * A floating-point number * A boolean You can store up to **50 key-value pairs**.
---@field subscription_id? string|distilled.Null ID of a subscription to upgrade. It must be on a free pricing. If checkout is successful, metadata set on this checkout will be copied to the subscription, and existing keys will be overwritten.
---@field success_url? string|distilled.Null URL where the customer will be redirected after a successful payment.You can add the `checkout_id={CHECKOUT_ID}` query parameter to retrieve the checkout session id.
---@field return_url? string|distilled.Null When set, a back button will be shown in the checkout to return to this URL.
---@field embed_origin? string|distilled.Null If you plan to embed the checkout session, set this to the Origin of the embedding page. It'll allow the Polar iframe to communicate with the parent page.
---@field locale? string|distilled.Null
---@field currency? polar.PresentmentCurrency|string|distilled.Null
