---@field custom_field_data? polar.CheckoutsUpdateRequestCustomFieldDataMap Key-value object storing custom field values.
---@field product_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the product to checkout. Must be present in the checkout's product list.
---@field amount? number|distilled.Null
---@field seats? number|distilled.Null Number of seats for seat-based pricing.
---@field units? number|distilled.Null Number of units for unit-based pricing.
---@field is_business_customer? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field customer_name? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_email? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_billing_name? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_billing_address? polar.AddressInput|distilled.Null
---@field customer_tax_id? string|distilled.Null
---@field locale? string|distilled.Null
---@field trial_interval? polar.TrialInterval|string|distilled.Null The interval unit for the trial period.
---@field trial_interval_count? number|distilled.Null The number of interval units for the trial period.
---@field metadata? polar.CheckoutsUpdateRequestMetadataMap Key-value object allowing you to store additional information. The key must be a string with a maximum length of **40 characters**. The value must be either: * A string with a maximum length of **500 characters** * An integer * A floating-point number * A boolean You can store up to **50 key-value pairs**.
---@field currency? polar.PresentmentCurrency|string|distilled.Null
---@field discount_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the discount to apply to the checkout.
---@field allow_discount_codes? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to allow the customer to apply discount codes. If you apply a discount through `discount_id`, it'll still be applied, but the customer won't be able to change it.
---@field require_billing_address? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to require the customer to fill their full billing address, instead of just the country. Customers in the US will always be required to fill their full address, regardless of this setting. If you preset the billing address, this setting will be automatically set to `true`.
---@field allow_trial? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to enable the trial period for the checkout session. If `false`, the trial period will be disabled, even if the selected product has a trial configured.
---@field customer_ip_address? string|distilled.Null
---@field customer_metadata? polar.CheckoutsUpdateRequestCustomerMetadataMap|distilled.Null Key-value object allowing you to store additional information that'll be copied to the created customer. The key must be a string with a maximum length of **40 characters**. The value must be either: * A string with a maximum length of **500 characters** * An integer * A floating-point number * A boolean You can store up to **50 key-value pairs**.
---@field success_url? string|distilled.Null URL where the customer will be redirected after a successful payment.You can add the `checkout_id={CHECKOUT_ID}` query parameter to retrieve the checkout session id.
---@field return_url? string|distilled.Null When set, a back button will be shown in the checkout to return to this URL.
---@field embed_origin? string|distilled.Null If you plan to embed the checkout session, set this to the Origin of the embedding page. It'll allow the Polar iframe to communicate with the parent page.

